{
 "_doc": "What each ground photograph shows, read by eye on contact sheets (2026-11-18), so the ground and the product line up (the owner: \"ideally bg and assets line up\"; DESIGN-LAW 145). shows: 'scene' (a world the product stands in: a landscape, a desk, a field, a texture; suits: the categories it fits) or 'product' (it shows goods itself: subject is the line or kind it shows, make and model where it is a vehicle or a phone, vehicle: pickup or van). floor: where a surface the product can stand on meets the eye, 0 to 1 of the photograph's height; FullAd frames a scene so this line is the foot of the product band. never: a reason the photograph is not used at all. The full ad's pools (scripts/build_full_grounds.mjs) and the recipes (scripts/build_recipes.mjs) read this table; each --check fails a ground it does not tag. A car photograph may list cuts: the cut-outs that are that very car (a model name can span generations or bodies: an E46 and a G80 M3, a Transit Connect and a Courier); only those stand on it. where: the place a photograph shows, where it can be told (a metro of motion/metros.js, or another place): an ad whose area is in a metro stands on no photograph of somewhere else (rule 161).",
